<Component>
    <Description>
        A mosfet. 
        
        If you give this Transistor a value that starts with "fuse", then this component has an internal fuse at the source,
        which simulates the destruction of the component, when maximal current "idmax" (in A) or maximal voltage "udsmax" (in V) is exceeded.
        
        The models are ignoring any parasitic capacity. When making high-frequency simulations, this might lead to biased results. 
        Also the maximum values are set to continuous max values, even though the fuse interrupts as soon as this max value is reached. Therefor the real component might survive conditions -especially when pulsed- where a "fuse"-model is interrupted by the fuse.You might want to change the values of idmax or udsmax  in these cases.
    </Description>
    <eeschema_sch>
        L Transistor_FET:2N7002
        ALIAS Transistor_FET:2N7002E Transistor_FET:2N7002H Transistor_FET:2N7002K
        DEFINE [udsmax] 60
        DEFINE [idmax] IF [model] ENDS_WITH 2 THEN 0.115 ELSEIF [model] ENDS_WITH E THEN 0.24 ELSEIF [model] ENDS_WITH H THEN 0.21 ELSE 0.38 ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF
        DEFINE [parameters]  nmos (vto=1.6 kp=.17 rd=0  is=.04p  )
